-- title:
--   Unramifiedness of O[e] at primes over mathfrak m_O
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring, let $M$ be a commutative domain equipped with an $O$-algebra structure, and assume the structure map $O \to M$ is injective. Let $e \in M$, and let $f \in O[X]$ be a monic polynomial with $f(e) = 0$ (evaluation via the algebra map) whose reduction along the residue map $O \to O/\mathfrak m_O$ is a separable polynomial over the residue field. Write $D := O[e]$ for the $O$-subalgebra of $M$ generated by the single element $e$, and let $P$ be a prime ideal of $D$ containing the ideal $\mathfrak m_O D$ generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $O$ under $O \to D$. The conclusion is the conjunction of two assertions about the localisation $D_P$ of $D$ at $P$: first, $D_P$ is a discrete valuation ring; second, the maximal ideal of the local ring $D_P$ equals the image in $D_P$ of the ideal $\mathfrak m_O D$, i.e. the extension $O \to D_P$ is unramified in the strong sense that a uniformiser of $O$ generates the maximal ideal of $D_P$.
--
--   This is the Kummer–Dedekind criterion in its local form: adjoining a root of a monic polynomial with separable reduction to a discrete valuation ring produces a ring whose localisations at the primes above $\mathfrak m_O$ are again discrete valuation rings with the same uniformiser. It serves as the arithmetic engine behind the constructions of unramified sub-discrete-valuation-rings used in the auxiliary level structures for modular curves, being cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_unramified_subDVR_adjoin_eq_top_of_ne`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_unramified_subDVR_adjoin_eq_top_of_ne) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_unramified_subDVR_adjoin_eq_top`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_unramified_subDVR_adjoin_eq_top).
